* TR-808 / Yocto v2.007 -- combined NGSpice full circuit (one circuit).
* All instrument branches share supply, models, IO buses and master stage as in
* the schematic (sheets CY, BD, IO, Master). New instruments are added HERE as
* another section, not as a separate file.
*
* Origin of the sections:
*  - Models, supply, CY/Ride blocks 1-9 and block 11: from the CY/Ride rebuild.
*    Only change: the TRIG_CY amplitude is the parameter trig_cy_amp
*    (default 5 = as before).
*  - HiHat (OH/CH): sheet HH (only the trigger amplitudes are parameters).
*    Shares bp2out with CY.
*  - BD: sheet BD, parts with suffix _bd, internal nets bd_n<NN>, supply
*    b2p/b2n (+B2/-B2).
*  - IO buses (sheet IO) and master stage U1 (sheet Master).
*  - SD (snare): sheet SD + NOISE, parts with suffix sd_/no_, internal nets
*    sd_n<NN>/no_n<NN>, supply SD: b3p/b3n (+B3/-B3, shared with HiHat U7),
*    NOISE: b4p/b4n (+B4/-B4, new).
*    Q35 (2SC828, noise source via the reverse-biased B-E junction, the same
*    documented technique as Q8 in the real TR-808): the breakdown itself is
*    modelled physically (D2SC828EB, Bv/Ibv from the verified 2SC828 datasheet
*    V(BR)EBO=7V @ Ie=10uA, two independent sources; the circuit's own DC
*    operating point hits the same value almost exactly). The noise AMPLITUDE
*    (TRNOISE), however, cannot be derived (pure shot noise at the bias current
*    would be ~6 orders of magnitude too small for this known avalanche /
*    microplasma mechanism) -- an explicit placeholder, not verified against
*    hardware. Pot taper VR7/VR8/VR9 not measured (linear placeholder,
*    sd_vr7/8/9).
* Known gaps (not modelled, not invented): Q82/Q83 (2SC2878, no verified
* model), Q79 bias network, jack / LEFT-RIGHT output path behind the Q82/Q83
* nodes, WN (snare noise source, see above), instruments other than
* CY/OH/CH/BD/SD (their bus resistors are tied to 0V on the source side,
* see the IO section).
* Assumption: cable J14 (IO) <-> J6 (Master) and J11/J13 <-> BD/CY/SD sheet
* connectors pin for pin 1:1.
* Parameters: bd_twidth (width of the TRIG_BD pulse, Yocto firmware 2 ms), trig_cy_amp / trig_bd_amp / trig_oh_amp / trig_ch_amp / trig_sd_amp (0 = not triggered;
* default OH/CH = 0, since they choke each other in the real machine),
* bd_vr4/bd_vr5/bd_vr6 / sd_vr7/sd_vr8/sd_vr9 (knob positions, sd_vr* taper
* unconfirmed), vr28 (master pot).
.param trig_cy_amp=5 trig_bd_amp=5 trig_oh_amp=0 trig_ch_amp=0 trig_sd_amp=5 bd_vr4=0.5 bd_vr5=0.5 bd_vr6=0.5 sd_vr7=0.5 sd_vr8=0.5 sd_vr9=0.5 vr28=0.5 bd_tdelay=20m bd_twidth=2m sd_tdelay=20m sd_twidth=2m trig_lt_amp=0 trig_mt_amp=0 trig_ht_amp=0 lt_vr10=0.5 lt_vr11=0.5 mt_vr12=0.5 mt_vr13=0.5 ht_vr14=0.5 ht_vr15=0.5 lt_tdelay=20m lt_twidth=2m mt_tdelay=20m mt_twidth=2m ht_tdelay=20m ht_twidth=2m lt_sw=1 mt_sw=1 ht_sw=1 trig_rm_amp=0 rm_vr16=0.5 rm_tdelay=20m rm_twidth=2m rm_sw=1 trig_hc_amp=0 hc_vr17=0.75 hc_tm3=0.60 hc_tdelay=20m hc_twidth=2m hc_sw=1 trig_cb_amp=0 cb_vr5=0.5 cb_tdelay=20m cb_twidth=2m trig_pc2_amp=0 pc2_vr1=0.5 pc2_vr2=0.5 pc2_vr3=0.5 pc2_vr18=0.5 pc2_vr19=0.5 pc2_vr20=0.5 pc2_tm5=0.5 pc2_sw2=1 pc2_sw3=1 pc2_tdelay=20m pc2_twidth=2m

* ---- Transistor models (level 1, part verification, completed) ----
* Q2SC945: final model (Bf=222.31, 7 NEC test cases <4% dev.).
.model Q2SC945 NPN(Bf=222.31 Is=35.1f Ise=6.63e-15 Ne=1.319 Ikf=130m Vaf=315 Tf=.5564n Rb=9.86 Rc=0.68 Cjc=6.4p Cje=20p Tr=10n Mjc=.330 Vjc=.75 Mje=.33 Vje=.75 Cjs=2p)
* Q2SA733: LTspice Standard.bjt, agrees with Renesas hFE(typ)=200.
.model Q2SA733 PNP(IS=55.9f BF=205 NF=1.01201 VAF=135 IKF=462.6m
+ ISE=180f NE=1.65 BR=2.048 NR=1.012
+ RB=20 RE=10m RC=1.7
+ CJE=35p VJE=900m MJE=500m TF=700p
+ XTF=10 VTF=10 ITF=700m
+ CJC=13p VJC=750m MJC=400m XCJC=500m
+ TR=10n XTB=2.00849 EG=1.11 XTI=3 FC=500m)
* D1N4148: verified against the official Nexperia SPICE model.
.model D1N4148 D(Is=4.352n N=1.906 Rs=0.6458 Cjo=0.7048p Vj=0.869 M=0.03 Tt=3.48n Bv=110 Ibv=100u)
* D1N34: germanium diode (Yocto value string 1N34 on D80-D85)
.model D1N34 D(IS=4e-07 N=1.8953 RS=77.292 CJO=1.058e-12 VJ=0.75 M=0.33 BV=65 IBV=1m)
* J2SK30: Toshiba 2SK30A rank Y (Yocto part Q74 on the RM sheet; the Roland service plan marks it 2SK30A (Y)). Sources: Idss rank Y 1.2-3.0 mA,
* Vgs(off) -0.4..-5.0 V, |Yfs| >= 1.2 mS, Ciss 8.2 pF / Crss 2.6 pF typ (XIAOSHENG 2SK30A datasheet, second source of the Toshiba part); Vto/Beta/Rd/Rs from
* the published 2SK30AY NJF model (T. Enzaka, LTspice standard.jft, Vto -1.4 V, Beta 1.1 mA/V^2), CGS/CGD recomputed from the datasheet Ciss/Crss with PB=1 V.
* Vto of the individual part is NOT resolved by the datasheet (rank bounds only) -- open point. Only NJF level-1 parameters (ngspice).
.model J2SK30 NJF(VTO=-1.4 BETA=1.1m LAMBDA=1m RD=30 RS=30 CGS=5.6p CGD=8.62p PB=1 IS=10f)
* PC-2 Q6 calibrated to the Yocto2 recordings (2026-10-07, 'PC-2 long.aif' decay envelope 0.1-0.8 s): effective Vto -0.54 V instead of -1.4 V (rank of the real part unknown); together with CPC27 3.32u (effective, 1.51 x 2.2u) 1.0 dB rms envelope error.
.model J2SK30PC2 NJF(VTO=-0.54 BETA=1.1m LAMBDA=1m RD=30 RS=30 CGS=5.6p CGD=8.62p PB=1 IS=10f)
* D2SC828EB: 2SC828 base-emitter junction, reverse breakdown ONLY (Q35 noise source,
* collector unconnected in the schematic -- see comment above). Bv/Ibv = V(BR)EBO=7V at
* Ie=10uA (two independent sources: components101/utmel republication of the Toshiba family;
* ST/Semtech 2SC828 datasheet cross-check, same value). Is/N/Rs are generic
* small-signal silicon placeholders, NOT characterised for this part -- irrelevant,
* since only the reverse branch is used here.
.model D2SC828EB D(Is=10f N=1.5 Rs=5 Bv=7 Ibv=10u)

* CD4584/MC14584B behavioural model. Threshold ratios CORRECTED
* (U4 open point): the previous version used the onsemi datasheet
* values measured at VDD=15V (VT+=8.0V/VT-=6.9V -> ratios 0.5333/0.46).
* In the CY circuit, however, U4 is really supplied from vdd4 (confirmed
* 4.7876V), not from 15V -- according to the datasheet the
* threshold ratios are NOT exactly independent of VDD (VT+/VDD=0.54 instead of
* 0.5333, VT-/VDD=0.42 instead of 0.46 at VDD=5.0V/25C typ, the table row
* closest to our real vdd4) -- taken directly from the datasheet table, no
* free fit / no interpolation. Hysteresis cross-check: 0.54-0.42=0.12,
* times VDD=5V gives 0.6V, exactly the separately tabulated typical VH value
* at VDD=5V -- internal consistency check passed.
.subckt SCHMITT4584 IN OUT VDD VSS
Bout OUT VSS V = (V(OUT,VSS)>0.5*V(VDD,VSS)) ? ((V(IN,VSS)>0.54*V(VDD,VSS)) ? 0 : V(VDD,VSS)) : ((V(IN,VSS)<0.42*V(VDD,VSS)) ? V(VDD,VSS) : 0)
.ends

* UPC4558_V3 op-amp terminal model (9 parameters
* verified individually against the NEC datasheet table G10518EJAV0DS00,
* all 0-0.36% dev.). Rout=196.08 Ohm is an unquantified placeholder
* (no datasheet value found), CMRR/PSRR/Isc not modelled
* (not effective with a clean DC supply and no interference, or no
* datasheet value available).
.subckt UPC4558_V3 INP INN OUT VCC VEE
.param P_ROUT=196.08
.param P_VOM_EMF_TARGET=14.275
.param P_VOM_EMF={P_VOM_EMF_TARGET-0.885}
Rib_p INP 0 1e12
Rib_n INN 0 1e12
Iib_p 0 INP {60n+5n/2}
Iib_n 0 INN {60n-5n/2}
Eoff INPoff 0 INP INN 1
Voff INPoff INNoff DC 0.5m
.param P_CMRR_RATIO=31622.8
.param P_C1=53p
.param P_GM={2*3.14159265*3Meg*P_C1}
.param P_R1={1e5/P_GM}
.param P_IMAX={1Meg*P_C1}
Bgin1 0 n1 I = {P_IMAX*tanh((P_GM/P_IMAX)*(V(INNoff)+((V(INP)+V(INN))/2)/P_CMRR_RATIO))}
R1 n1 0 {P_R1}
C1 n1 0 {P_C1}
.model DCLAMP D(Is=1e-20 N=1 Rs=1)
.param P_VOM_HEADROOM_HI={15-P_VOM_EMF}
Dclamp_hi n1 vout_hi DCLAMP
Vout_hi vout_hi VCC DC {-P_VOM_HEADROOM_HI}
Dclamp_lo vout_lo n1 DCLAMP
Vout_lo vout_lo VEE DC {P_VOM_HEADROOM_HI}
Eout n2 0 n1 0 1
Rout n2 OUT {P_ROUT}
.ends UPC4558_V3

* AN6912 (Panasonic AN1339 datasheet, LM339 class): quadruple comparator, one channel per subcircuit, open-collector output.
* Datasheet typical values (VCC=5V table): voltage gain 200 V/mV (RL=15k) -> tanh transition width Vw = (VCC-VEE)/2/200000 at the 15 V supply used here;
* output low VOL=0.2 V at ISINK=3 mA -> saturated on-resistance 0.2 V / 3 mA; output leakage 0.1 nA at 5 V. Not modelled (datasheet gives no typical
* or a value only as a bound): input offset (2 mV typ, sign unknown), input bias current (250 nA max only), response time 1.3 us, ISINK 10 mA min.
.subckt AN6912_CMP INP INN OUT VCC VEE
BSINK OUT VEE I={(3m/0.2)*V(OUT,VEE)*0.5*(1+tanh((V(INN)-V(INP))/(15/2/200000)))}
RLEAK OUT VEE 50G
.ends AN6912_CMP
* BA6110 (ROHM BA6110FS datasheet, VCA/OTA with buffer; the SIP9 part of the Yocto library has the same pin functions). Pins: INP = positive input,
* INN = negative input, CTRL = control input (datasheet pin 7), OUT = VCA output (pin 11, current output), BUFIN = buffer input (pin 12),
* BUFOUT = buffer output (pin 14), BIAS = input bias diode pin (pin 5), VCC, VEE.
* Datasheet equations: control current Icontrol flows into CTRL and is the tail current of the input pair, Av = gm*Ro = Icontrol/52mV * Ro (Fig.8,
* no diode bias: checked against the 27k curve, 34.3 dB at 100 uA), differential input pair -> output current Icontrol*tanh(Vd/52mV).
* BIAS is not connected inside this model: with the pin held at VEE (as on the Yocto HC sheet) no diode bias current flows (Id = 0, the Fig.8 condition).
* CTRL pin: diode-connected NPN to VEE (Fig.1: control pin current mirror), modelled with the verified Q2SC945 Vbe (datasheet gives no Vbe value).
* Buffer: unity-gain follower (Fig.1: NPN/PNP emitter follower, VF cancelled) with the 11 kOhm resistor from VCC to BUFOUT stated in the datasheet.
* Not modelled (no typical value in the datasheet): input offset (3 mV max), input bias/buffer input current (0.8 uA), output impedance of the current
* output, buffer output impedance, output voltage limits (VOM6 14 V typ, VOM8 11 V typ: checked afterwards on the simulated nodes).
.subckt BA6110_OTA INP INN CTRL OUT BUFIN BUFOUT BIAS VCC VEE
VCM CTRL CX 0
QC CX CX VEE Q2SC945
BO VEE OUT I={I(VCM)*tanh((V(INP)-V(INN))/52m)}
EBUF BUFOUT 0 BUFIN 0 1
RBUF BUFOUT VCC 11k
.ends BA6110_OTA

* ---- Supply rails (per schematic: b4rail/b1rail +15V,
* b4railn -15V (supply of U3), vee=-B1* -15V (supply of U5/U6,
* own net node per netlist) -- the CY sheet netlist itself
* contains no local decoupling (C24/C25/R78/R79 are on another
* sheet), hence not included here). ----
VB4 b4rail 0 DC 15
VB4N b4railn 0 DC -15
VB1 b1rail 0 DC 15
VVEE vee 0 DC -15
* +B2/-B2 (BD sheet) and +B5*/-B5* (Master, U1): same convention as the
* other rails (ideal +/-15V behind the 0R links of the PSU-Buss sheet)
VB2P b2p 0 DC 15
VB2N b2n 0 DC -15
VB5P b5p 0 DC 15
VB5N b5n 0 DC -15
* +B4/-B4 (NOISE sheet, feeds Q35 noise bias/U24): same convention. Own
* source names (VB4NOP/VB4NON), since VB4/VB4N are already used for b4rail/b4railn (CY).
VB4NOP b4p 0 DC 15
VB4NON b4n 0 DC -15
* +B6/-B6 (HT sheet, U18): same convention
VB6P b6p 0 DC 15
VB6N b6n 0 DC -15
* +B7/-B7 (RM sheet, U19-U21): same convention
VB7P b7p 0 DC 15
VB7N b7n 0 DC -15
* +B8/-B8 (HC sheet, Q65-Q73, U22, U23): same convention
VB8P b8p 0 DC 15
VB8N b8n 0 DC -15
* +B9/-B9 (PC-2 sheet, U8/U10/U11/U25/U27/U9): same convention
VB9P b9p 0 DC 15
VB9N b9n 0 DC -15

* ---- Boundary conditions TRIG_CY/ACCENT_CY (off-sheet inputs, not
* part of the CY sheet itself).
* ACCENT_CY: (Yocto_v2_003beta/Dio.ino SetDacA(),
* milliVolt=map(velocity,0,127,0,4090), confirmed by calculation from the
* MCP4822 gain mechanism, held stable by sample & hold with a TL074 buffer);
* 0.9*4.09V=3.681V corresponds to velocity 0.9 in the reference runs.
* TRIG_CY: CORRECTED -- pulse width was wrongly 1ms,
* in reality (Yocto_v2_003beta/Clock.ino:112 AND Seq.ino:509, both trigger
* paths identical) exactly 2ms between setting and resetting the trigger bit
* in the 74HC595 (IC112). 5V amplitude confirmed (HC series on a 5V
* supply). ----
Vtrigcy trig_cy_ext 0 PWL(0 0 1u 0 2u {trig_cy_amp} 2.001m {trig_cy_amp} 2.002m 0 4 0)
Vaccentcy accent_cy_ext 0 DC 3.681
* TRIG_BD: same 74HC595 path, 5V/2ms; ACCENT_BD as ACCENT_CY (DAC A, 0.9 -> 3.681V)
Vtrigbd trig_bd 0 PWL(0 0 {bd_tdelay} 0 {bd_tdelay+1u} {trig_bd_amp} {bd_tdelay+bd_twidth+1u} {trig_bd_amp} {bd_tdelay+bd_twidth+2u} 0 4 0)
Vaccentbd accent_bd 0 DC 3.681
* TRIG_SD: same 74HC595 path, 5V/2ms; ACCENT_SD as ACCENT_CY/BD (DAC A, 0.9 -> 3.681V)
Vtrigsd trig_sd 0 PWL(0 0 {sd_tdelay} 0 {sd_tdelay+1u} {trig_sd_amp} {sd_tdelay+sd_twidth+1u} {trig_sd_amp} {sd_tdelay+sd_twidth+2u} 0 4 0)
Vaccentsd accent_sd 0 DC 3.681
* TRIG_LT/MT/HT: 74HC595 path, 5V/2ms; ACCENT_* = 3.681V like the other voices
Vtriglt trig_lt 0 PWL(0 0 {lt_tdelay} 0 {lt_tdelay+1u} {trig_lt_amp} {lt_tdelay+lt_twidth+1u} {trig_lt_amp} {lt_tdelay+lt_twidth+2u} 0 4 0)
Vaccentlt accent_lt 0 DC 3.681
Vtrigmt trig_mt 0 PWL(0 0 {mt_tdelay} 0 {mt_tdelay+1u} {trig_mt_amp} {mt_tdelay+mt_twidth+1u} {trig_mt_amp} {mt_tdelay+mt_twidth+2u} 0 4 0)
Vaccentmt accent_mt 0 DC 3.681
Vtright trig_ht 0 PWL(0 0 {ht_tdelay} 0 {ht_tdelay+1u} {trig_ht_amp} {ht_tdelay+ht_twidth+1u} {trig_ht_amp} {ht_tdelay+ht_twidth+2u} 0 4 0)
Vaccentht accent_ht 0 DC 3.681
* TRIG_RM: 74HC595 path, 5V/2ms; ACCENT_RM = 3.681V like the other voices
Vtrigrm trig_rm 0 PWL(0 0 {rm_tdelay} 0 {rm_tdelay+1u} {trig_rm_amp} {rm_tdelay+rm_twidth+1u} {trig_rm_amp} {rm_tdelay+rm_twidth+2u} 0 4 0)
Vaccentrm accent_rm 0 DC 3.681
* TRIG_HC: 74HC595 path, 5V/2ms; ACCENT_HC = 3.681V like the other voices
Vtrighc trig_hc 0 PWL(0 0 {hc_tdelay} 0 {hc_tdelay+1u} {trig_hc_amp} {hc_tdelay+hc_twidth+1u} {trig_hc_amp} {hc_tdelay+hc_twidth+2u} 0 4 0)
Vaccenthc accent_hc 0 DC 3.681
* TRIG_CB: 74HC595 path, 5V/2ms; ACCENT_CB = 3.681V like the other voices
Vtrigcb trig_cb 0 PWL(0 0 {cb_tdelay} 0 {cb_tdelay+1u} {trig_cb_amp} {cb_tdelay+cb_twidth+1u} {trig_cb_amp} {cb_tdelay+cb_twidth+2u} 0 4 0)
Vaccentcb accent_cb 0 DC 3.681
* TRIG_PC2: 74HC595 path, 5V/2ms; ACCENT_PC2 = 3.681V like the other voices
Vtrigpc2 trig_pc2 0 PWL(0 0 {pc2_tdelay} 0 {pc2_tdelay+1u} {trig_pc2_amp} {pc2_tdelay+pc2_twidth+1u} {trig_pc2_amp} {pc2_tdelay+pc2_twidth+2u} 0 4 0)
Vaccentpc2 accent_pc2 0 DC 3.681

* ==== Block 1: trigger front end Q2/Q6/Q19 ====
R3 trig_cy_ext n517 22k
R6 n517 0 10k
Q2 n519 n517 0 Q2SC945
R10 n519 n516 4.7k
R15 n516 accent_cy_ext 4.7k
Q6 n515 n516 accent_cy_ext Q2SA733
R83 n515 0 22k
R84 n515 q19base 10k
Q19 q19coll q19base q19emit Q2SC945
R85 q19coll b85mid 100
R86 b85mid b1rail 100
C35 b85mid 0 47u

* ==== Block 1: VDD4 regulator Q9/R60/R61/C12 (R60 fix: base n311 -> GND) ====
R61 b4rail n311 10k
R60 n311 0 5.6k
Q9 b4rail n311 vdd4 Q2SC945
C12 vdd4 0 100u
* Rload4: U4's supply current from vdd4, derived from the onsemi
* MC14584B datasheet Rev.10 (IT = 1.8uA/kHz*f + IDD at VDD=5V, note 5
* for CL<>50pF: IT(CL)=IT(50pF)+(CL-50)*V*f*k, k=0.001), applied
* per gate with the oscillator frequencies already measured (
* 500-900Hz, independent of VDD since it is a pure threshold ratio) and
* the real timing capacitors C1-C6 (10-22nF, NOT the 50pF test
* condition) instead of the negligible pure IDD quiescent-current
* order of magnitude (0.0005-0.0015uA). Sum over all 6 gates =
* 308.76uA at V=5V/CL=Cx -> R=V/I=15.5k as substitute load, NO free
* fit, directly from the datasheet formula + already measured values.
* Without this load U4 draws no current at all from vdd4 in this model
* (Bout is an ideal voltage source, see the SCHMITT4584 subckt) -- Q9 would
* have nothing to regulate and vdd4 would stay at any arbitrary initial
* value (even a wrong one).
Rload4 vdd4 0 15.5k

* ==== Block 2: CD4584 hex oscillator (U4 gates A-F) ====
* Gate C (R40=560k/C1=18n)
Xu4c n_c osc_c vdd4 0 SCHMITT4584
C1 n_c 0 18n
R40 osc_c n_c 560k

* Gate B (R41=560k/C2=10n)
Xu4b n_b osc_b vdd4 0 SCHMITT4584
C2 n_b 0 10n
R41 n_b osc_b 560k

* Gate A (R42=680k/C3=10n)
Xu4a n_a osc_a vdd4 0 SCHMITT4584
C3 n_a 0 10n
R42 osc_a n_a 680k

* Gate D (R43=220k/C4=18n)
Xu4d n_d osc_d vdd4 0 SCHMITT4584
C4 n_d 0 18n
R43 osc_d n_d 220k

* Gate E (trimmed: osc_e -> R45=100k -> n308 -> TM2 rheostat (S->E,
* 0..220k depending on tm2_pos, A pin unused per netlist) -> n_e,
* C5=18n at n_e). tm2_pos = factory-alignment trimmer position, not yet
* determined (placeholder 0.5).
* tm2_pos CORRECTED: real factory-alignment calibration from
* "Yocto v2.0 Building Manual.pdf" p.23 ("Cowbell oscillator frequency:
* Set TM2* to get 588Hz at TP7" -- label in the manual is misleading,
* TP7 is unambiguously osc_e/gate E on the CY sheet per the netlist).
* Back-calculated from f=2.0699/(RC) (corrected
* thresholds): tm2_pos=0.4344, cross-checked by SPICE: 588.2Hz (target
* 588Hz, <0.1% deviation). Replaces the earlier placeholder 0.5.
* CORRECTED AGAIN (HiHat session 2026-09-14): 588.2Hz was
* Yocto's OWN building-manual calibration (for the Yocto target device), not
* necessarily the frequency of the real TR-808 reference unit (serial 103852)
* whose recordings serve as the listening reference. Log-frequency-shift
* cross-correlation (bias-free, no combination model)
* on TWO independent HiHat signals (OH/CH, both fed from this shared
* oscillator bank) showed consistently: SPICE was +7.4% (OH) and
* +3.2% (CH) too high. -5% on TM1 AND TM2 together lowered both to
* <0.2% residual deviation AND improved the absolute correlation (OH:
* 0.478->0.508, CH: 0.578->0.637) -- both trimmers in the same direction,
* both independent voices confirm the same amount: not a random
* fit. tm2_pos=0.4809 -> 558.79Hz (target 558.8Hz, <0.01% deviation).
.param tm2_pos=0.4809
Xu4e n_e osc_e vdd4 0 SCHMITT4584
C5 n_e 0 18n
R45 osc_e n308 100k
Rtm2 n308 n_e {220k*tm2_pos}

* Gate F (trimmed: osc_f -> R44=150k -> n309 -> TM1 rheostat (S->E,
* 0..220k depending on tm1_pos) -> n_f, C6=22n at n_f).
* tm1_pos CORRECTED: real factory-alignment calibration from
* "Yocto v2.0 Building Manual.pdf" p.23 ("Cowbell oscillator frequency:
* Set TM1* to get 390Hz at TP6" -- label in the manual is misleading, TP6
* is unambiguously osc_f/gate F on the CY sheet per the netlist).
* Back-calculated from f=2.0699/(RC): tm1_pos=0.4148, cross-checked by
* SPICE: 389.9Hz (target 390Hz, <0.1% deviation). Replaces the earlier
* placeholder 0.5.
* CORRECTED AGAIN (HiHat session 2026-09-14): see the detailed
* reasoning at tm2_pos above -- the same -5% correction, confirmed by the
* same two independent OH/CH measurements.
* tm1_pos=0.4728 -> 370.40Hz (target 370.4Hz, exact).
* CALIBRATED TO THE YOCTO2 RECORDINGS (2026-10-03): C6 = 10n instead of 22n (schematic/board say 22n), tm1_pos=0.4132.
* Finding: the reference recordings show the upper cowbell line at about 859 Hz (gate F); with 22n and the schematic's part values
* 859 Hz is not reachable (370 Hz). C6 10n + TM1 0.4132 -> 859 Hz (calculation from 857.91 Hz at 0.4146). Gate E (558.8 Hz) fits unchanged.
* Cross-check CY/OH/CH (shift correlation against the Yocto2 recordings, mean, at s=1): CY 0.527 -> 0.722, OH 0.465 -> 0.630, CH 0.656 -> 0.778 (48 kHz).
.param tm1_pos=0.4132
Xu4f n_f osc_f vdd4 0 SCHMITT4584
C6 n_f 0 10n
R44 osc_f n309 150k
Rtm1 n309 n_f {220k*tm1_pos}

* ==== Block 3: summing of the 6 oscillators -> vsumnode ====
R35 osc_c vsumnode 120k
R37 osc_b vsumnode 120k
R39 osc_a vsumnode 120k
R46 osc_d vsumnode 120k
R48 osc_e vsumnode 120k
R50 osc_f vsumnode 120k
R53 vsumnode 0 1k

* ==== Block 4: EG#1.1/EG#1.2 ====
D8 q19emit c41node D1N4148
* C41 (EG#1.1 decay capacitor of the cymbal) = 1.2u, SCHEMATIC 1u: calibrated to the Yocto2 recordings CY-1..CY-20 (2026-10-04). NGSpice at decay pot maximum / tone 1.0: t-20 dB / t-40 dB = 1315 / 2220 ms with 1u,
* 1960 / 3295 ms with 1.5u (proportional to C41); the longest recording (CY-20) has 1585 / 2950 ms -> 1.2u (E12 value, ~1580 / 2660 ms).
C41 c41node 0 1.2u
* VR2 (2MB): per netlist A=GND, E+S bridged to the same node
* (true rheostat, not a voltage divider) -- decay_knob = user decay knob position, not yet
* backed by a concrete target value (placeholder 0.5).
.param decay_knob=0.5
R93 c41node vr2wiper 470k
Rvr2 vr2wiper 0 {2Meg*decay_knob}
Q20 b1rail c41node q20emit Q2SC945
R105 q20emit c45node 33k
C45 c45node 0 2.2u
R104 c45node d12a 22k
D12 d12a d12k D1N4148

