* ==== Block 9: band 1 buffer (Q25), mesh, U6-A (terminated), U6-B (CY_OUT) ====
C48 d12a nodex 1.5n
C59 nodex q25base 1.5n
R127 q25base 0 82k
Q25 b1rail q25base q25emit Q2SC945
C58 q25emit r123node 10n
R123 r123node r121node 100k
R121 r121node meshx1 10k
C57 r121node 0 3.3n
R124 nodex q25emit 22k
R126 q25emit vee 22k

C56 u5bout n120node 10n
R120 n120node meshx1 10k
C55 u5aout n112node 10n
R112 n112node meshx2 22k
R129 meshx1 meshx3 15k
R119 meshx2 meshx3 22k
* VR4 (20KB, 3-terminal divider, wiper=S=GND): modelled as two resistors
* A->GND and E->GND (each the share of the track on the respective side of
* the wiper), .param instead of fixed 0.5.
.param tone_knob=0.5
R125 meshx1 vr4e 2.2k
RvR4e_internal vr4e 0 {20k*tone_knob}
RvR4a meshx2 0 {20k*(1-tone_knob)}

* U6-A: unused, correctly terminated op-amp half (
* +IN=GND, -IN=OUT as voltage follower) -- no signal path.
Xu6a 0 n481 n481 b1rail vee UPC4558_V3

* U6-B: last real amplifier stage before CY_OUT.
C90 meshx3 u6bn 10n
R118 u6bp 0 47k
R128 u6bout u6bn 470k
C77 u6bout u6bn 220p
* VR6 (100KA) as rheostat: A=u6bout, E+S bridged (u6bm). "100KA" means
* taper A (logarithmic/audio). The manufacturer of the pot is not documented
* (the kit's front-panel pots are bundled separately, not on the public BOM),
* so the curve is a representative one: the 15A (JIS.A) curve of the
* Song Huei R0903N, whose footprint (2.5mm pin pitch) matches the Yocto board
* exactly. Eleven points read from the manufacturer's taper sheet
* (0/10/.../100% rotation -> 0/1/2.5/5.5/10.5/16/26/40/65/93/100% resistance),
* used as piecewise linear interpolation, not a functional fit. The Bourns
* PTV "A" curve (15% at 50% rotation) and a TT Electronics curve bracket it
* from both sides, i.e. three independent sources converge. The individual
* curve of the original part is not available; it is treated as part
* tolerance of the A-taper class (up to 4.52dB, ~68%, at vr6_pos<=0.2,
* <1dB at vr6_pos>=0.5). The real knob position is unknown (VR6 is a
* front-panel control, not a factory-alignment trimmer), so
* vr6_pos=0.5 remains the only sensible model value.
.param vr6_pos=0.5
.param vr6frac = {
+ (vr6_pos<=0.1) ? (0.0    + (vr6_pos-0.0)/0.1*(0.01-0.0))    :
+ (vr6_pos<=0.2) ? (0.01   + (vr6_pos-0.1)/0.1*(0.025-0.01))  :
+ (vr6_pos<=0.3) ? (0.025  + (vr6_pos-0.2)/0.1*(0.055-0.025)) :
+ (vr6_pos<=0.4) ? (0.055  + (vr6_pos-0.3)/0.1*(0.105-0.055)) :
+ (vr6_pos<=0.5) ? (0.105  + (vr6_pos-0.4)/0.1*(0.16-0.105))  :
+ (vr6_pos<=0.6) ? (0.16   + (vr6_pos-0.5)/0.1*(0.26-0.16))   :
+ (vr6_pos<=0.7) ? (0.26   + (vr6_pos-0.6)/0.1*(0.40-0.26))   :
+ (vr6_pos<=0.8) ? (0.40   + (vr6_pos-0.7)/0.1*(0.65-0.40))   :
+ (vr6_pos<=0.9) ? (0.65   + (vr6_pos-0.8)/0.1*(0.93-0.65))   :
+                  (0.93   + (vr6_pos-0.9)/0.1*(1.0-0.93))    }
Rvr6 u6bout u6bm {100k*vr6frac}
C78 u6bm u6bn 33u
Xu6b u6bp u6bn u6bout b1rail vee UPC4558_V3
* R166: last real output resistor before connector J4
* (CY_OUT).
R166 u6bout cy_out 1k

* ==== HiHat (sheet HH): OH/CH, verbatim from hihat_rebuild/hihat_both_4s.cir (trigger amplitudes as parameters) ====
* =====================================================================
* POT3 subckt removed (2026-09-14): it was faulty, "C" is the
* housing ground lug of the pot (symbol POT_GND, a circle icon), NOT
* the third electrical resistance terminal (the real 3-terminal
* resistor has only A/E/S, symbol POT_EU-). E and S are tied to the same node
* in the schematic -> pure rheostat A->wiper, no ground path through the pot itself.

Vb3p b3p 0 DC 15
Vb3n b3n 0 DC -15

* Boundary conditions TRIG_OH/TRIG_CH/ACCENT_OH/ACCENT_CH -- now REALLY
* derived, no longer taken over from CY:
*
* TRIG: IC112 (74*595, sheet 0) is a 16-bit shift register (2x74HC595
* cascaded), QA=TRIG_CY, QB=TRIG_OH, QC=TRIG_CH, QD=TRIG_PC2 --
* verified by net search. define.h: CY=bit8, OH=bit9, CH=bit10 (matches
* QA/QB/QC of the high byte exactly). Clock.ino: SetDoutTrig(stepValue)
* writes ALL bits (incl. OH/CH) in ONE SPI transfer, then ALWAYS
* `delayMicroseconds(2000)` (firmware source line, not interpreted),
* then ResetDoutTrig() resets all bits together -- TRIG_OH and
* TRIG_CH therefore PROVABLY (not assumed) have the same 2ms/5V
* pulse shape as TRIG_CY, because of the identical shift-register
* latch mechanism. Fired here SEPARATELY each (not simultaneously) for
* separate OH/CH reference runs.
*
* ACCENT: IC110 (TL074, sheet 0) -- per the netlist ACCENT_OH and ACCENT_CH are
* the SAME electrical connection (both at IC110 -IN/OUT) --
* OH and CH share ONE sample & hold accent voltage (Clock.ino:
* SetMux()/SetDacA() is called once per step for the currently active
* instrument, DAC channel A as with CY). Modelled here with
* the same value 3.681V (=0.9 velocity)
* on BOTH nets -- no fitting, same derivation as
* ACCENT_CY.
Vtrigoh_hh trig_oh 0 PWL(0 0 1u 0 2u {trig_oh_amp} 2.001m {trig_oh_amp} 2.002m 0 4 0)
Vtrigch_hh trig_ch 0 PWL(0 0 1u 0 2u {trig_ch_amp} 2.001m {trig_ch_amp} 2.002m 0 4 0)
Vaccoh_hh accent_oh 0 DC 3.681
Vaccch_hh accent_ch 0 DC 3.681

RH1  n566 trig_oh   22k
RH8  0 n566         10k
QH3  n568 n566 0    Q2SC945
RH12 n568 n567      22k
QH7  n569 n567 accent_oh  Q2SA733
RH17 n567 accent_oh 4.7k
RH2  n559 trig_ch   22k
RH7  0 n559         10k
QH4  n562 n559 0    Q2SC945
RH11 n562 n560      22k
QH8  n563 n560 accent_ch  Q2SA733
RH16 n560 accent_ch 4.7k
RH13 0 n563          22k
RH130 0 n331     10k
RH131 n331 n569  22k
QH21  n576 n331 0  Q2SC945
Rvr3  b3p n360 1Meg
RH132 n576 n360  100k
RH133 n575 n576  10k
QH22  n574 n575 0  Q2SC945
QH23  n574 n580 0  Q2SC945
RH173 n580 n581  330k
CH60  n576 0     10u
RH134 n574 n573  100k
RH135 n572 n569   10k
QH24  n571 n572 n573  Q2SC945
* CH62 (OH decay storage) = 0.82u, SCHEMATIC 0.47u: calibrated to the Yocto2 recordings OH-1..OH-7 (2026-10-04). With 0.47u the decay time saturates at 375 ms (t-20 dB) and the envelope sags;
* the recordings reach 595 ms with a plateau and a steep end. 0.82u (standard value): Rvr3 2.1M -> 620 ms, plateau of OH-4..OH-7 within 1.4-2.2 dB.
