* ==== IO buses (sheet IO) and master stage (sheet Master) ====
* Each channel hangs on the two buses through two resistors (N$847 = busr,
* N$812 = busl). Source side: BD -> bd_out, CY -> cy_out, OH (tip contact TN) -> oh_out,
* CH (ring contact RN of the OH/CH jack) -> ch_out. All other channels
* (instruments not simulated) have their source side at 0V -- their outputs
* are low-impedance op-amp outputs without signal. Tip contact: 10n to GND
* (C500 BD, C508 CY, C509 OH, C502 SD) or ring contact (C514 CH); normal contact (TN) without plug connected to T.
C500 bd_out 0 10n
C502 sd_out 0 10n
* C506: HANCLAP jack tip (HC sheet CP_MA_OUT via J12-3), R516/R517 = normal-contact resistors to busr/busl
C506 hc_out 0 10n
* C507: COWBELL jack tip (CB sheet CB_OUT via J12-4), R519/R520 = normal-contact resistors to busr/busl
C507 cb_out 0 10n
* C510: PC-2 jack tip (PC-2 sheet CP_MA_OUT1 via J13-4), R528/R529 = normal-contact resistors to busr/busl
C510 pc2_out 0 10n
* C8: RIMSHOT jack tip (RM sheet), R55/R56 = normal-contact resistors to busr/busl
C8 rm_out 0 10n
C504 ht_out 0 10n
C505 mt_out 0 10n
C503 lt_out 0 10n
C508 cy_out 0 10n
C509 oh_out 0 10n
C514 ch_out 0 10n
R502_io bd_out busl 12k
R505_io sd_out busl 12k
R508_io lt_out busl 15k
R511_io ht_out busl 8.2k
R514_io mt_out busl 12k
R517_io hc_out busl 12k
R520_io cb_out busl 12k
R523_io cy_out busl 8.2k
R526_io oh_out busl 15k
R529_io pc2_out busl 12k
R535_io ch_out busl 15k
R56_io rm_out busl 12k
R501_io bd_out busr 12k
R504_io sd_out busr 12k
R507_io lt_out busr 8.2k
R510_io ht_out busr 15k
R513_io mt_out busr 12k
R516_io hc_out busr 12k
R519_io cb_out busr 12k
R522_io cy_out busr 15k
R525_io oh_out busr 8.2k
R528_io pc2_out busr 12k
R536_io ch_out busr 8.2k
R55_io rm_out busr 12k
* Bus -> J14 -> J6 (pin 3 = busr, pin 1 = busl) -> C253/C254 (10u) -> U1B/U1A -IN.
* Summing amplifier U1 (uPC4558C, model UPC4558_V3), feedback VR28 (50KB, rheostat
* between output and -IN, both halves coupled), +IN to GND.
C253 busr u1b_inn 10u
C254 busl u1a_inn 10u
XU1B 0 u1b_inn u1b_out b5p b5n UPC4558_V3
XU1A 0 u1a_inn u1a_out b5p b5n UPC4558_V3
Rvr28b u1b_out u1b_inn {max(50k*vr28,1)}
Rvr28a u1a_out u1a_inn {max(50k*vr28,1)}
* U1 outputs -> R474/R473 (1k) -> C255/C252 (10u) -> node J6-5/J6-6 (Q82/Q83 collectors,
* Q82/Q83 not modelled) -> J14-5/-6 -> R530/R532 (2.2k) -> R531/R533 (10k) || C511/C512 (10n).
R474 u1b_out n778 1k
C255 n778 j6_5 10u
R473 u1a_out n779 1k
C252 n779 j6_6 10u
R530 j6_5 lout 2.2k
R531 lout 0 10k
C511 lout 0 10n
R532 j6_6 rout 2.2k
R533 rout 0 10k
C512 rout 0 10n

* ==== Block 11: virtual recording coupling (2026-09-13)
* -- NOT a TR-808/Yocto part ====
* In steady state u6bout has a real, non-zero DC operating point
* (-0.0245872V, from the op-amp Voff/Ibias fix -- a physically
* real property of THIS node, not a model error). According to the Eagle schematic (sheet IO, see the block 10
* comment) the real master-out path itself has NO series coupling
* capacitor -- only the individual "CYMBAL" jack carries C508 (10nF),
* which is not in the signal path in normal operation (no plug inserted, master out is what is heard).
* The DC offset is therefore really present at the
* master-out pin as well. It does not end up in ANY real reference recording
* (CY1050.WAV etc.), because every device used for recording (audio
* interface / mixer input) has an AC-coupled line input --
* industry standard, present almost without exception. To make our rendered
* reference WAV fairly comparable with a real recording,
* a single-pole virtual AC-coupling
* high-pass is attached HERE -- explicitly OUTSIDE the actual circuit, purely
* as a model of the recording chain. Corner frequency ~10.6Hz (far below any audio content
* of the cymbal/ride signals, but fast enough to settle within ~100ms
* -- lies entirely within the attack window that has already been thoroughly
* checked). Part values NOT backed by the schematic (no
* real part), chosen deliberately.
* For information only, the tap BEFORE this stage (ioMasterR/ioMasterL,
* block 10) remains unchanged in the real, DC-afflicted state
* -- for internal circuit-fidelity comparisons (SPICE node against
* a reduced-model tap) that remains the right quantity, the offset belongs THERE
* and must be the same on BOTH sides. u6bout_ac is intended only for the direct
* comparison with real hardware recordings.
Cacrec u6bout u6bout_ac 15u
Racrec u6bout_ac 0 1k

