* Solver settings for the long run: Gear integration and a 20 us maximum step.
* With the default settings a run of more than ~0.5 s can stop with
* "Timestep too small" (at the idle PC-2 JFET). .save keeps only the dumped nodes
* (all ~1150 nodes would not fit into memory).
.options method=gear
.save v(cy_out) v(bd_out) v(sd_out) v(busr) v(busl) v(u1a_out) v(u1b_out) v(bd_n53) v(bd_n55) v(bd_n56)
.tran 20u 4 0 20u uic

* Outputs: cy_out, bd_out, sd_out, oh_out, ch_out
.control
run
wrdata tr808_full_nodes.txt v(cy_out) v(bd_out) v(sd_out) v(busr) v(busl) v(u1a_out) v(u1b_out) v(bd_n53) v(bd_n55) v(bd_n56)
.endc
.end
